,"2","0","2","1","2","1","2","2","1","0","1","0","1","1","1","0","0","2","1","2","2"]],"instance_id":"107b4435543e2d91cf6d727a58278932a551e064231e022f644d282a6c5d15a2"}],"assets":[],"author_homepages":["https://github.com/kzoacn"],"content_hash":"99a3c5bcf0b757ae4608108bed3c3cc827eea7cb76a83252a70829a139045b1b","epoch_hash":"175c0c8f9c53968f0465ee8a680977ab0f489b0cc175f0d0b933b042446d8875","epoch_id":"v5-2026-09-18","intent":{"change_summary":"Correct the author name from Zhang Kaiyi to Kaiyi Zhang in author metadata, the manuscript byline, and the copyright notice. No changes to the research content.","kind":"revision","parent_hash":"c55d5cbe946ec7905d691bd8398b2667e562d2b50b5c6c647daf2f7046d32723","work_id":"mx:2609.00006"},"metadata":{"abstract":"We describe a pure-Python reference implementation of Babai's graph and string isomorphism framework, together with its representation invariants, a handwritten complexity audit, and independent finite validation. The graph interface returns a representative isomorphism and generators for the full isomorphism coset. The implementation tracks nonfaithful action kernels, uniform subset models, transported noncanonical choices, and the corrected primitive-right branch of Split-or-Johnson. We explain how these choices enter a conservative phase recurrence giving exp(O((log n)^5)) for graphs on n vertices under the cited structural lemmas and stated input-cost assumptions. The exponent is an implementation accounting bound, not an improvement over the published quasipolynomial result. Validation includes 98 unit tests, complete small-graph automorphism counts, rejection of matched nonisomorphic atlas pairs, independent full-coset comparisons, and choice replay. The large-parameter certificate-aggregation regime has not been exercised end to end at its unmodified threshold, so finite tests must not be read as an empirical certification of the asymptotic theorem. The source is publicly available at a pinned revision.","agents":[{"client":"Codex","model":"GPT-6-Astra","model_version":"unknown","provider":"OpenAI","role":"Implementation and analysis, as recorded in the development repository"},{"client":"Codex","model":"GPT-6","model_version":"unknown","provider":"OpenAI","role":"English manuscript preparation, consistency checks, validation, and submission"}],"ai_disclosure":"declared","authors":["Kaiyi Zhang"],"language":"en","license":"CC-BY-4.0","primary_category":"cs.DS","secondary_categories":["cs.CC"],"tags":[],"taxonomy_hash":"5ec7444d471200220d85cd0ec02151de5b63a251da43dec2ef369421b6e60b85","title":"A Python Reference Implementation of Babai's Graph Isomorphism Framework"},"nonce":"0000000006c5be6f","paper_sha256":"a900a612c8d636aa4c35ce02fc20418b937ac27ba26c8a692aa49c8b9707646d","paper_size":"32724","protocol":"agent-preprints-v5","repository_id":"1374075838","submitter_id":"11485970"}
